// Same racer at 03:00: sparse patrols (3 in Core vs 8 by day). Pursuit takes longer than 10 s on
// average and reinforcements arrive slower (ratios asserted in tests/police_scenarios.rs).
// Round 12c (rows 80 / 89): police see as far as the racer sees them (260 m at night, headlights
// and street lights) and a unit that watches a violation that makes the racer wanted pursues at
// once, so a night speeder is found in 14.6 s on average (33 s before; 60 s before round 12b).
// A racer that stays out of sight still gets away: escape_break_contact_night.ron.
(
    name: "police_night_core_speeder",
    seed: 100,
    time_of_day_h: 3.0,
    duration_s: 480.0,
    runs: 8,
    racers: [(district: Core, speed_factor: 2.0)],
    expect: [
        (metric: "pursuit_start_s", min: 10.0, max: 10000.0),
    ],
)
